eaders whose values are absent from the environment secret inventory.                                                                                              | Redact credential headers in errors, attachments, and output, including headers split across output chunks; retain useful failure diagnostics.                                                    | Resolved in assembly 6b4b263b: ANSI and split-header regressions pass; the full functional and documentation reruns pass. Final-layer evidence remains separately tracked.                                                                                                                                                                        |\\n383:| F-212 | Medium   | Browser route ownership and database fixtures can outlive their contexts or pools, skip later cleanup after a failure, or leave partial setup.                                                                        | Observe actual context closure, drain started operations, acquire fixture groups atomically, and attempt every owned cleanup before ending its pool.                                              | Resolved in assembly: native context closure and prior ownership fixes retain their earlier functional proof. Remaining URL/concurrency fixtures now own atomic setup, drain operations and preserve cleanup; current strict typing, 1,674 server and 123 PostgreSQL tests pass with zero owned fixture tenants or active/idle transactions left. |\\n384-| F-213 | Medium   | An uncertain checkout offers a creation retry that the server rejects and cancellation copy that implies the held reservation can be released.                                                                        | Explain the payment-review block, preserve the claim and reservation, and retain normal ready-checkout payment and cancellation.                                                                  | Resolved in assembly 4dd644: canonical add-on review copy, organizer approval capability and platform confirmation guards pass full server/app suites and all 167 functional tests. Held payment claims remain intact; financial recovery policy is unchanged.                                                                                    |\\n385-| F-214 | High     | Registration discount checks accept a discount type with a null discounted price, including confirmed registrations.                                                                                                  | Require a non-null discounted price whenever a discount is recorded, preserving valid zero-price and undiscounted snapshots.                                                                      | In progress: baseline proves the missing rejection; repaired full PostgreSQL suite passes all 111 tests; final-layer verification pending.                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\\n386-| F-215 | Medium   | Shell-wrapped provider test scripts discard user arguments, so `--list` can unexpectedly run the full selected suite.                                                                                                 | Forward every argument as a distinct shell argument while retaining canonical preflight and project selection.                                                                                    | Resolved in assembly 6b4b263b: all nine isolated shell regressions and the complete Auth0/Maps and live ESNcard commands pass. Final-layer verification remains separately tracked.                                                                                                                                                               |\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ad849a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004417,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":29,\"output\":\"{\\\"status\\\": \\\"running\\