ged.\",\n    \"events RPC contract adds only three validators and replaces list limit/offset/startAfter schemas. Parent direct-transfer removals, nullable typed check-in timing issue/new mutation error, and required nullable ESN input remain.\",\n    \"No17B announcementRoleIds/hasRegistrationOptions/userIsCreator/requiresSignIn fields are introduced by these merges. Event unlisted/includeUnlisted remain supported at17A; template default fields stay retired in inherited16S sources.\",\n    \"All24 before/after hashes match frozen manifest and every before matches frozen16R parent; approved paused/schedule/scroll chaining for nonmerged paths is bound by owner manifest, not independently re-reviewed in this pass.\"\n  ],\n  \"verification\": \"Only source reads, source diff comparison and SHA256/text inventory. No parser/compiler/lint/formatter/tests/runtime/DB/provider/network/refs or source edits. This receipt is sole write.\"\n}\n383:| F-212 | Medium   | Browser route ownership and database fixtures can outlive their contexts or pools, skip later cleanup after a failure, or leave partial setup.                                                                        | Observe actual context closure, drain started operations, acquire fixture groups atomically, and attempt every owned cleanup before ending its pool.                                              | Resolved in assembly: native context closure and prior ownership fixes retain their earlier functional proof. Remaining URL/concurrency fixtures now own atomic setup, drain operations and preserve cleanup; current strict typing, 1,674 server and 123 PostgreSQL tests pass with zero owned fixture tenants or active/idle transactions left. |\n"},"started_at_ms":1788571335904,"completed_at_ms":1788571335904}}
