{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:24:13.514Z","ordinal":20136,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-af923003-f32f-4745-b631-47ad2b5aec8c","process_id":"27909","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg --files layer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal | rg 'root|review|independent' | head -40 && sed -n '1,60p' review-progress.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto-stack-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"list_files","cmd":"rg --files layer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal","path":"pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg 'root|review|independent'","query":"root|review|independent","path":null},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,60p' review-progress.md","name":"review-progress.md","path":"review-progress.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"layer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/sourceowner-independent-review.json\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/assembly/root-review.json\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/before.ts\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/manifest.json\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/after.ts\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/typed-contract.patch\n# Replacement stack review\n\nThe replacement stack is local and incomplete. Nothing has been pushed, no pull request has changed, and nothing has been deployed. Original heads remain preserved: #123 `951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f` and #124 `d3688389a91075041786fe001aba10e15847abc9`. The last verified remote base is `d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea`; publication requires a fresh remote check.\n\n## Local stack\n\n| Layer | Exact commit | Paths against parent | Ordinary local CI gates |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n| 00 `00-runtime-security` | `9acc1f36719341e9517e65a9ff2a56538398d3a8` | 15 | All fresh ordinary +151 functional/+52 docs pass; cleanup independently verified |\n| 01 `01-retire-legacy-import` | `3ad029b3b8fd705974bfa438b0e548fe67cf0f45` | 73 | All fresh ordinary +151 functional/+52 docs pass; cleanup verified |\n| 02 `02-local-runtime` | `08806f0be682290375bd9c1c398494dd86402652` | 47 | Fresh changed-tree gates pending |\n| 03 `03-client-foundations` | `d957893ae7c5ab95850520b88334be557fdedce3` | 87 | Fresh changed-tree gates pending |\n| 04 `04-verified-identity` | `75580cce90bffe42539eefceb001c4b63ec5e63d` | 59 | Fresh changed-tree gates pending |\n| 05 `05-request-routing` | `d010202fcdacb10ef11cd489deaca11ad7ac2d03` | 95 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 06 `06-organization-settings` | `9acc8e24c42b0621d9468e9acf5aad033a5646d3` | 84 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 07 `07-provider-results` | `5b5c0eb7b780ffbdb5972e2e07ea1e0eacfede57` | 37 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 08 `08-roles-members-audit` | `f46c903e0c320a50d5fe69cf5f14676474014d34` | 79 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 09 `09-registration-integrity` | `49295bc28f9f0870e2aa3a7c80cfec9eaddbbccd` | 66 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 09b `09b-input-bounds` | `a48681d964369e621ad42039e60fe792a9280284` | 72 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 10 `10-payment-setup` | `2297b8faaea808c8bec13f2c2a68cc0de66253af` | 97 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 11 `11-email-delivery` | `c2efc93225f26886ee1fc3560530fcf98d15cadd` | 37 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 12a `12a-registration-engine` | `36f1e5b28f59b4512d0237ae89ae7e07cdf6eb13` | 62 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 12b `12b-registration-presentation` | `5144d4455c50b1527535e90dba6d2b4491d59ced` | 52 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 13 `13-private-ticket-transfers` | `f447de92c84e9607bbefbba28dc7915131d2bedc` | 77 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 14 `14-checkin-and-scanner` | `8eeca34f6746579d019a85604bde3a4acd792182` | 45 | Identical tree; evidence rebinding and image/runtime pending |\n| 15 `15-event-authoring` | `2a1283ab0ca5ac3a84442037f89384f4150594c9` | 72 | External candidate source checks pass; all actual-head ordinary and runtime gates pending |\n\nThe chain is registered locally with gh-stack. Every sealed layer is below 100 changed paths. [Current ref inventory](current-local-stack.json) and [PR draft manifest](pr-drafts/manifest.json) bind actual parent diffs and source identities. Draft descriptions through14 have17 entries and now bind the replayed refs. Prior ordinary results are historical until the required new-head checks or approved content-evidence supplements complete. The complete source, unit, PostgreSQL, infrastructure and strict production-image receipts are retained for [06](layer06-19241-verification.md), [07](layer07-9377-verification.md) and [08](layer08-5da93c-verification.md), alongside the earlier layer receipts. These are not claims of branch-authentic Browser or provider acceptance. The repository also requires full functional and documentation suites in the normal local PR baseline; their per-prefix evidence is tracked in [the publication inventory](publication-gate-inventory-00-14.json). The first exact layer00 invocation finished151 collected/138 passed/13 failed; documentation did not start, and all owned processes/resources/ports were cleaned. All13 failures report the same signing-secret resolver timeout. Layer00 introduced distroless while its helper still executed cat. The existing later Bun reader is now moved into00 and all18 stack refs have been replayed and independently verified. Changed00–04 trees require fresh gates. Full trees05–15 are verified identical to their prior versions. Repaired00 now passes source, full unit, PostgreSQL and infrastructure checks; its canonical image passes with308 targets and zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings. The exact repaired00 run passes151 functional and52 documentation tests. Its wrapper records a PermissionError during the final supervisor probe; independent native process, Docker resource and port checks confirm complete owned cleanup. The original failed wrapper receipt remains intact, and the successful suites are accepted separately in [root acceptance](prefix-runtime-verification/runs/00-9acc1f36-a1/root-acceptance-and-cleanup.json). Historical strict/unit/PostgreSQL evidence for05–14 may be explicitly rebound only under [the recorded content-evidence policy](prefix-runtime-verification/post-replay-gates/root-content-evidence-policy.json), with fresh activation, infrastructure, image and runtime checks. Actual15 gates remain pending.\n\nLayer 09 binds event, template, discount and saved-answer ownership and historical registration prices. Its first full server run exposed a release-note source guard mismatch and an eager database-view import cycle. The correction preserves the view SQL in a separate module; all four focused files / 14 tests pass. All ordinary gates pass at corrected 5c510416, including 194 server files / 1,574 tests, 124 app files / 898 tests, 18 PostgreSQL files / 103 tests, both infrastructure roots and the strict production-image scan. The image is 95,760,503 bytes with zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings including unfixed entries. The original failures and correction remain in the [receipt](layer09-5c510-verification-evidence.json). Its [handoff](layer-09-registration-integrity.md) explains schema impact. The next child, 09b, carries quantity/text limits together with API and editor validation. Payment account/tax work (10) now passes every ordinary gate at corrected e41291ae: 1,642 server tests, 937 app tests, 129 PostgreSQL tests and the strict production-image scan. Its failed predecessor is retained. Independent price-display changes were moved to 12b so the corrected layer remains 97 paths. Generic email/worker work (11) has passed its full server/app and PostgreSQL suites; its first production image build stalled after bundle output and was explicitly interrupted with its evidence retained. An unchanged environmental retry passes the complete canonical gate in 225.651 seconds: a 95,770,352-byte runtime and zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings including unfixed entries. The underlying reason for the first stall remains unproven. Later large concerns will be split where needed to preserve the file limit and understandable scope.\n\nLayer 12a is a clean 62-path registration-engine checkpoint at `dab0f1d5cecd1a0656ad2e480dc41e637075400b`. Its corrected PostgreSQL suite passes all 152 tests in 20 files, with zero owned URL-race tenants or active/idle transactions remaining. Both Terraform roots validate and infrastructure scanning reports zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings. All ordinary gates now pass: 1,718 server tests, 974 app tests and a first-attempt production-image scan with zero HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities. The verified local PR draft is included in the14-entry manifest through12a. Earlier stale-copy and incomplete-fixture failures remain recorded. Layer12b is materialized as52paths at corrected `f0481bf0`; strict47roots/277sources0, all1,718server/991app tests and both infrastructure roots pass. PostgreSQL20/152 and the first production-image attempt are also green, including unfixed HIGH/CRITICAL findings. Its final draft is in the15-entry local manifest through12b. Layer 13 is corrected at `81dc5672d0887017584f6f16b2ee256e0cdf37fe`, with 77 paths against 12b. The earlier 73-path head and its eight stale-caller failures are retained. Fresh corrected-head source checks, strict typing (61 roots / 409 sources / zero diagnostics), all 1,691 server tests, 1,008 app tests, 166 PostgreSQL tests and both infrastructure roots pass. Owned fixture and transaction readback is empty. The canonical production-image check passes on its first attempt, with zero HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities across 296 targets including unfixed entries. Root independently verified all 77 before/after source blobs and 11 raw logs. Its final local draft brings the manifest to 16 entries; final Browser/docs/provider acceptance remains separate.\n\nLayer 14 is corrected at `eddd110f1606e34a48e92d97a13e83ea4a7cfea4`, with 45 files against corrected 13. The initial 44-file head passed strict, app, PostgreSQL and infrastructure checks but exposed two obsolete source assertions in the full server suite; those failures remain retained. The correction preserves every test case and replaces the retired list-cap assertion with explicit single-ticket lookup and tenant-boundary checks. Fresh corrected-head strict typing (35 roots / 258 sources / zero diagnostics), all 1,698 server tests, 1,028 app tests, 174 PostgreSQL tests and both infrastructure roots pass. Fixture/transaction readback is empty. The canonical image passes after correcting checkout permissions without changing source bytes or relaxing scan flags: 95,778,395 bytes and zero HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities across 296 targets including unfixed entries. Root independently verified all 45 before/after blobs and 11 raw logs. The final local draft is entry 17 in the manifest; final Browser/docs/provider acceptance remains separate.\n\nCanonical checks explicitly use Node 24.15.0 from NVM and Bun 1.3.14. The Homebrew node@24 alias resolves to a different major version and is not accepted as runtime evidence. Image scans include unfixed HIGH/CRITICAL findings; database update checks remain enabled. [Earlier provenance supplement](layer00-04-node-provenance.md).\n\n## Current application checkpoint\n\nThe assembly is clean at `56e7fdc90802f8478b2d56eb6de88bf1db01bac7` (tree `811989533a546642300de116e91822d053cd4576`). Its 14-file profile, cache, row-removal and truthful-copy checkpoint passes all1,674 server tests,1,342 app tests and123 PostgreSQL tests, with zero diagnostics across8 strict roots and104 first-party sources. Lint, format, release-note and diff checks pass; fixture/transaction readback is empty. [Checkpoint evidence](assembly-profile-complete-checkpoint.json) binds final code bytes to the passing source and PostgreSQL snapshots. The failed lint, stale permission fixture and disabled-button fixture assumption are retained with their corrections. F228 profile/card lifetime and home/offline copy, F231 stable row tracking and F232 current-value cache updates are complete at this source checkpoint. Fresh complete assembly runtime, Browser and documentation publication remain pending. No app runtime or Pages preview is running.\n\nThe prior authoring checkpoint `8ca0b13bd03186a2689898d35bc4525e6024d4ad` retains its25-file source/PG proof in [its receipt](assembly-authoring-complete-checkpoint.json): all nine authoring components, sibling-read lifetime fixes and F230 retained event paging, with1,674server/1,308app/123PG tests passing.\n\nThe preceding clean assembly head `948dc033c508c9249d3e7f0096a43e2c856b1d12` (tree `b50e8562db84df2b18b25cdb809d66edfd293654`) records the 16-path feedback/fixture/documentation batch. All 1,674 server tests, 1,185 app tests and 123 PostgreSQL tests pass; the 12-root/191-source strict graph has zero diagnostics. Final lint, format and diff checks pass. The source-equivalent committed bytes and retained failures are bound in [checkpoint evidence](assembly-feedback-checkpoint.json). Its new runtime/publication acceptance remains pending. The prior app runtime and Pages preview are stopped; all exact-project app containers, networks and volumes are removed. The previous generated Pages catalog is preserved in a verified212-file archive, and only its owned generated roots were restored to the clean upstream consumer for regeneration.\n\nClean test head `4dd644f784ccb534effb838656634f083d282206` now passes all 167 functional tests, 51 documentation tests, 11 Auth0/Google Maps integration tests and nine live ESNcard release tests plus nine provider-error unit cases, with no retries or incomplete tests. It corrects one stale add-on transfer-message assertion; the prior 166/167 failure remains recorded. The runtime was built from `c5f8a1b10a6e03a896dad7694c57c851c61f6d4c`; the one-file comparison proves that application, server, schema, dependencies and build inputs are unchanged. The [runtime receipt](assembly-4dd644-runtime-gates.json) records both identities and all log hashes. The complete combined documentation publication also passes54/54 and installs13 guides into an isolated Pages checkout. Its 19 tooling tests, lint, diff check and production build pass under the separate pinned Pages runtime (Node 24.11.0/Bun 1.3.14). The installed catalog contains 13 guides and 199 PNGs with 203 references, no missing or unused images, and no retired output. Search and guide navigation work in the production preview, and the neutral email crop passes visual review. Final visual acceptance remains held: F-229 records a stale prior approval notification in the missing-file receipt screenshot. A separate companion anchor-offset issue is under review. The exact installed output has a verified local archive. That prior owned app runtime has now been stopped and its exact project resources removed.\n\nThe preceding implementation checkpoint is `c5f8a1b10a6e03a896dad7694c57c851c61f6d4c` (33 changed paths). Payment review copy, normalized copied transfer codes, locked check-in timing, transferred add-on reads, copied paid-template checks and fixture ownership repairs pass 1,674 server tests, 1,172 app tests and 123 PostgreSQL tests. The final 24-root strict graph has zero diagnostics. Exact source hashes retain the earlier app/PG results across the last test-only additions, and database readback confirms no owned RLS objects or fixture tenants remain. [Clean source receipt](assembly-ticket-fixture-final-source.json). Its production runtime is the verified source-equivalent runtime for the complete 4dd644 acceptance above.\n\nThe previous complete runtime checkpoint is the clean assembly head `5d49f011c4d6f467c3d74d0241b99173f5a6f87f`. It adds audit-specific microsecond cursors, readable audit descriptions, effective role details and a durable wildcard rename/revocation journey. Full server tests pass 214 files / 1,671 tests, app tests 145 / 1,148, and PostgreSQL tests 20 / 115. The 11-root strict graph has zero diagnostics, and audit fixture readback is empty. [Current receipt](assembly-5d49-verification-evidence.json).\n\nManual Browser acceptance at this head confirms that role details display effective wildcard grants, a name-only save preserves both stored wildcards, and explicitly revoking Manage payments preserves every other grant after reload. The temporary role was unassigned throughout and exact cleanup readback is zero. [Browser evidence](assembly-5d49-role-browser-evidence.json). Full functional acceptance passes 165 / 165, documentation 51 / 51, Auth0/Google Maps integration 11 / 11, and live ESNcard certification 9 / 9 plus all nine provider-error unit tests. There are no retries or incomplete tests. The owned server was gracefully stopped afterward, and all containers in its exact project are confirmed removed. [Complete runtime gate receipt](assembly-5d49-runtime-gates.json).\n\nThe later clean `30ab75c416569dbf3854ab839b08757f242e31ea` checkpoint adds participant input limits, template description feedback and cancellation of stalled email response bodies. All 214 server files / 1,672 tests and 145 app files / 1,152 tests pass. The strict check covers six edited roots and 225 sources with zero diagnostics, using the project's actual test ambient types. A rebuilt production runtime passes all ten collected registration/add-on Browser tests (seven setup tests and three journeys), including repeated guest clamping, the exact answer boundary and the original successful signup/readback. Its owned containers, network and volumes are removed. [Checkpoint receipt](assembly-input-email-checkpoint.json). These focused results do not replace the full final-stack runtime acceptance.\n\nThe previous clean `6b4b263b` checkpoint passed 164 functional tests, 51 documentation tests, 11 Auth0/Google Maps integration tests, nine live ESNcard tests and nine provider-error unit cases, all without retries. [Previous complete runtime receipt](assembly-6b4b-verification-evidence.json). Those results are historical evidence and do not certify the later head.\n\nThe fixture cleanup work preserves 1,549 assertions, 95 test titles and 247 screenshot/documentation calls while registering cleanup before writes and making scenario setup transactional. [Preservation evidence](assembly-f212-preservation.json). Route teardown, reporter redaction and shell argument-forwarding repairs retain their focused regression receipts. Earlier failed runs remain available with their source and cause; sensitive diagnostics have owner-only permissions.\n\n## Material findings and repairs\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"layer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/sourceowner-independent-review.json\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/assembly/root-review.json\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/before.ts\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/manifest.json\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/after.ts\nlayer17b-event-discovery/pg-fixture-lifetime-proposal/root-typed-followup/typed-contract.patch\n# Replacement stack review\n\nThe replacement stack is local and incomplete. Nothing has been pushed, no pull request has changed, and nothing has been deployed. Original heads remain preserved: #12