its and can remain eligible after the existing closing deadline.                                                                                              | Read the existing check-in clock after the registration and event locks, preserving the current opening and closing window.                                                                       | Resolved: check-in reads its clock after both locks. The actual SQL-adapter lock-wait regression passes in the full 1,674-test server suite; the original opening and closing policy is preserved.                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n+| F-226 | Medium   | Add-on handout details are blocked after ticket ownership transfers while a refund is pending or failed, even though ordinary use is allowed.                                                                         | Use the existing ownership-handoff blocking states for reads and preserve tenant, owner and expiration checks.                                                                                    | Resolved: the read guard and six PostgreSQL status cases pass the full 123-test database suite. Current owner, tenant and expiration checks remain enforced; refund and handout mutation policies are unchanged.                                                                                                                                                                             |\n+| F-227 | Medium   | Create-event-from-template checks paid sign-up options but omits paid add-ons copied from the template when payment setup is unavailable.                                                                             | Block submission with an explanation for any copied paid option or add-on while retaining every saved price.                                                                                      | Resolved